# Default branch requires signed commits
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::Repository assets)
# CTN: github_branch_protection
# Frameworks: KSI-SVC-VRI, KSI-AFR-UCM, NIST SI-7, CMMC SI.L2-3.14.1

META
    esp_id `github-branch-protection-requires-signed-commits-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `medium`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::Repository`

    title `Default branch requires signed commits`
    description `Validates that the default branch protection rule requires signed commits. Without this requirement, attackers with write access can spoof commit authorship and undermine commit-level non-repudiation.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,sdlc,branch-protection,commit-signing,ksi-svc-vri,ksi-afr-ucm,nist-si-7,cmmc-si-l2-3.14.1`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-SVC-VRI,KSI:KSI-AFR-UCM,NIST-800-53:SI-7,CMMC:SI.L2-3.14.1`
    control_objective `KSI-SVC-VRI,KSI-AFR-UCM,SI.L2-3.14.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:sdlc-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Settings, Branches, Branch protection rules: enable "Require signed commits" on the default branch rule. Coordinate with contributors first so they configure GPG, SSH, or S/MIME signing on their commits before enabling.`

    component_id `comp-github-sdlc`

    impl_KSI_SVC_VRI `Commit-level resource integrity is enforced by requiring all commits on the default branch to carry a verified cryptographic signature. The protection rules required_signatures.enabled flag must be true; absent or false fails the policy. The CTN observes the live setting via GitHub API at scan time.`
    impl_KSI_AFR_UCM `Use of cryptographic modules for commit attestation is bound at the platform layer. GitHub validates signature material (GPG, SSH, S/MIME) server-side and tags each commit with verified-or-unverified status. The branch protection rule requires the verified status on every commit reaching the default branch.`
    impl_SI_L2_3_14_1 `System and information integrity for source-control artifacts is enforced by mandating cryptographic signing of every commit on the default branch. The policy detects when this requirement is disabled and emits a finding.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder values, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. The VARs are pattern-fillers consumed by the template
    # OBJECT below; on bind, PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one
    # OBJECT per bound asset, each carrying that asset's concrete
    # owner / repo / branch from inventory.assets.metadata.
    VAR owner string `_unbound_`
    VAR repo string `_unbound_`
    VAR branch string `_unbound_`

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_repos union
        OBJECT repo_target
            owner VAR owner
            repo VAR repo
            branch VAR branch
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE protection_requires_signed
        found boolean = true
        protection_exists boolean = true
        requires_signed_commits boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_branch_protection
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF protection_requires_signed
            SET_REF github_repos
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
